{"id": "ch35", "number": "35", "title": "Properties of relations", "titleInlines": [{"type": "text", "text": "Properties of relations"}], "part": "VI", "blocks": [{"type": "para", "children": [{"type": "text", "text": "Symbolization keys allow us to assign two-place predicate symbols like ‘"}, {"type": "math", "latex": "R(x,y)", "display": false}, {"type": "text", "text": "’ to English predicates with two gaps, e.g., ‘"}, {"type": "math", "latex": "\\underline{\\hspace{2em}}_{x}"}, {"type": "text", "text": " is older than "}, {"type": "math", "latex": "\\underline{\\hspace{2em}}_{y}"}, {"type": "text", "text": "’. This allows us to symbolize arguments such as:"}]}, {"type": "list", "kind": "earg", "items": [{"children": [{"type": "para", "children": [{"type": "text", "text": "Rudolf is older than Kurt."}]}]}, {"children": [{"type": "para", "children": [{"type": "text", "text": "Kurt is older than Julia."}]}]}, {"label": [{"type": "text", "text": "∴"}], "children": [{"type": "para", "children": [{"type": "text", "text": "Rudolf is older than Julia."}]}]}]}, {"type": "para", "children": [{"type": "text", "text": "This argument is valid, but its symbolization in FOL,"}]}, {"type": "list", "kind": "earg", "items": [{"children": [{"type": "para", "children": [{"type": "math", "latex": "R(r,k)", "display": false}]}]}, {"children": [{"type": "para", "children": [{"type": "math", "latex": "R(k,j)", "display": false}]}]}, {"label": [{"type": "text", "text": "∴"}], "children": [{"type": "para", "children": [{"type": "math", "latex": "R(r,j)", "display": false}]}]}]}, {"type": "para", "children": [{"type": "text", "text": "is not. That’s because the validity of the argument depends on a property of the relation ‘"}, {"type": "math", "latex": "x", "display": false}, {"type": "text", "text": " is older than "}, {"type": "math", "latex": "y", "display": false}, {"type": "text", "text": "’, namely that if some person "}, {"type": "math", "latex": "x", "display": false}, {"type": "text", "text": " is older than a person "}, {"type": "math", "latex": "y", "display": false}, {"type": "text", "text": ", and "}, {"type": "math", "latex": "y", "display": false}, {"type": "text", "text": " is also older than "}, {"type": "math", "latex": "z", "display": false}, {"type": "text", "text": ", then "}, {"type": "math", "latex": "x", "display": false}, {"type": "text", "text": " must be older than "}, {"type": "math", "latex": "z", "display": false}, {"type": "text", "text": ". This property of ‘older than’ is called "}, {"type": "define", "term": "transitivity", "children": [{"type": "text", "text": "transitivity"}]}, {"type": "text", "text": ". We can symbolize this property "}, {"type": "emph", "children": [{"type": "text", "text": "itself"}]}, {"type": "text", "text": " in FOL as:"}]}, {"type": "displaymath", "latex": "\\forall x\\forall y\\forall z(( R(x,y) \\land R(y,z)) \\rightarrow R(x,z))"}, {"type": "para", "children": [{"type": "text", "text": "Whenever the validity of an argument "}, {"type": "emph", "children": [{"type": "text", "text": "only"}]}, {"type": "text", "text": " depends on a property of a relation involved, and this property can be symbolized in FOL, we can add this symbolization to the argument and obtain an argument that is in fact valid in FOL:"}]}, {"type": "list", "kind": "earg", "items": [{"children": [{"type": "para", "children": [{"type": "math", "latex": "\\forall x\\forall y\\forall z(( R(x,y) \\land R(y,z)) \\rightarrow R(x,z))", "display": false}]}]}, {"children": [{"type": "para", "children": [{"type": "math", "latex": "R(r,k)", "display": false}]}]}, {"children": [{"type": "para", "children": [{"type": "math", "latex": "R(k,j)", "display": false}]}]}, {"label": [{"type": "text", "text": "∴"}], "children": [{"type": "para", "children": [{"type": "math", "latex": "R(r,j)", "display": false}]}]}]}, {"type": "para", "children": [{"type": "text", "text": "Properties of relations such as transitivity are important concepts especially in applications of logic in the sciences. For instance, order relations between numbers such as "}, {"type": "math", "latex": "<", "display": false}, {"type": "text", "text": " and "}, {"type": "math", "latex": "\\le", "display": false}, {"type": "text", "text": " (and also "}, {"type": "math", "latex": ">", "display": false}, {"type": "text", "text": " and "}, {"type": "math", "latex": "\\ge", "display": false}, {"type": "text", "text": ") are transitive. The identity relation "}, {"type": "math", "latex": "=", "display": false}, {"type": "text", "text": " is also transitive."}]}, {"type": "para", "children": [{"type": "text", "text": "There are other properties of relations that are important enough to have names, and often show up in applications. Here are some:"}]}, {"type": "factoid", "children": [{"type": "list", "kind": "factoiditems", "items": [{"children": [{"type": "para", "children": [{"type": "text", "text": "A relation "}, {"type": "math", "latex": "R", "display": false}, {"type": "text", "text": " is "}, {"type": "define", "term": "transitive", "children": [{"type": "text", "text": "transitive"}]}, {"type": "text", "text": " iff it is the case that whenever "}, {"type": "math", "latex": "R(x,y)", "display": false}, {"type": "text", "text": " and "}, {"type": "math", "latex": "R(y,z)", "display": false}, {"type": "text", "text": " then also "}, {"type": "math", "latex": "R(x,z)", "display": false}, {"type": "text", "text": "."}]}]}, {"children": [{"type": "para", "children": [{"type": "text", "text": "A relation "}, {"type": "math", "latex": "R", "display": false}, {"type": "text", "text": " is "}, {"type": "define", "term": "reflexive", "children": [{"type": "text", "text": "reflexive"}]}, {"type": "text", "text": " iff for any "}, {"type": "math", "latex": "x", "display": false}, {"type": "text", "text": ", "}, {"type": "math", "latex": "R(x,x)", "display": false}, {"type": "text", "text": " holds."}]}]}, {"children": [{"type": "para", "children": [{"type": "text", "text": "A relation "}, {"type": "math", "latex": "R", "display": false}, {"type": "text", "text": " is "}, {"type": "define", "term": "symmetric", "children": [{"type": "text", "text": "symmetric"}]}, {"type": "text", "text": " iff whenever "}, {"type": "math", "latex": "R(x,y)", "display": false}, {"type": "text", "text": " holds, so does "}, {"type": "math", "latex": "R(y,x)", "display": false}, {"type": "text", "text": "."}]}]}, {"children": [{"type": "para", "children": [{"type": "text", "text": "A relation "}, {"type": "math", "latex": "R", "display": false}, {"type": "text", "text": " is "}, {"type": "define", "term": "anti-symmetric", "children": [{"type": "text", "text": "anti-symmetric"}]}, {"type": "text", "text": " iff for no two "}, {"type": "emph", "children": [{"type": "text", "text": "different"}]}, {"type": "text", "text": " "}, {"type": "math", "latex": "x", "display": false}, {"type": "text", "text": " and "}, {"type": "math", "latex": "y", "display": false}, {"type": "text", "text": ", "}, {"type": "math", "latex": "R(x,y)", "display": false}, {"type": "text", "text": " and "}, {"type": "math", "latex": "R(y,x)", "display": false}, {"type": "text", "text": " both hold."}]}]}]}]}, {"type": "para", "children": [{"type": "text", "text": "We have already seen that transitivity can be symbolized in FOL. The others can, too:"}]}, {"type": "list", "kind": "itemize", "items": [{"children": [{"type": "para", "children": [{"type": "math", "latex": "R", "display": false}, {"type": "text", "text": " is reflexive: "}, {"type": "math", "latex": "\\forall x\\, R(x,x)", "display": false}]}]}, {"children": [{"type": "para", "children": [{"type": "math", "latex": "R", "display": false}, {"type": "text", "text": " is symmetric:"}]}, {"type": "displaymath", "latex": "\\forall x\\forall y( R(x,y) \\rightarrow R(y,x))"}]}, {"children": [{"type": "para", "children": [{"type": "math", "latex": "R", "display": false}, {"type": "text", "text": " is anti-symmetric:"}]}, {"type": "displaymath", "latex": "\\lnot\\exists x\\exists y(( R(x,y) \\land R(y,x)) \\land \\lnot x=y)"}, {"type": "para", "children": [{"type": "text", "text": "or, equivalently,"}]}, {"type": "displaymath", "latex": "\\forall x\\forall y(( R(x,y) \\land R(y,x)) \\rightarrow x=y)"}]}]}, {"type": "para", "children": [{"type": "text", "text": "Relations expressing an equivalence in some respect are reflexive, e.g., ‘is the same age as’, ‘is as tall as’, and the most stringent equivalence of them all, identity "}, {"type": "math", "latex": "=", "display": false}, {"type": "text", "text": ". They are also symmetric: e.g., whenever "}, {"type": "math", "latex": "x", "display": false}, {"type": "text", "text": " is as tall as "}, {"type": "math", "latex": "y", "display": false}, {"type": "text", "text": ", then "}, {"type": "math", "latex": "y", "display": false}, {"type": "text", "text": " is as tall as "}, {"type": "math", "latex": "x", "display": false}, {"type": "text", "text": ". In fact, relations that are reflexive, symmetric, and transitive are called "}, {"type": "define", "term": "equivalence relations", "children": [{"type": "text", "text": "equivalence relations"}]}, {"type": "text", "text": "."}]}, {"type": "para", "children": [{"type": "text", "text": "Equivalences aren’t the only symmetric relations. For instance, ‘is a sibling of’ is symmetric, but it is not reflexive (as no one is their own sibling)."}]}, {"type": "para", "children": [{"type": "text", "text": "Relations that are reflexive, transitive, and anti-symmetric are called "}, {"type": "define", "term": "partial orders", "children": [{"type": "text", "text": "partial orders"}]}, {"type": "text", "text": ". For instance, "}, {"type": "math", "latex": "\\le", "display": false}, {"type": "text", "text": " and "}, {"type": "math", "latex": "\\ge", "display": false}, {"type": "text", "text": " are partial orders. The relation ‘is no older than’, by contrast, is reflexive and transitive, but not anti-symmetric. (Two different people can be of the same age, and so neither is older than the other.)"}]}], "exercises": [{"letter": "A", "blocks": [{"type": "para", "children": [{"type": "text", "text": "Give examples of relations with the following properties:"}]}, {"type": "list", "kind": "compactlist", "items": [{"children": [{"type": "para", "children": [{"type": "text", "text": "Reflexive but not symmetric"}]}], "id": "ch35.A.1", "formulas": [], "solution": [{"type": "para", "children": [{"type": "math", "latex": "\\underline{\\hspace{2em}}_{x}"}, {"type": "text", "text": " is no older than "}, {"type": "math", "latex": "\\underline{\\hspace{2em}}_{y}"}]}]}, {"children": [{"type": "para", "children": [{"type": "text", "text": "Symmetric but not transitive"}]}], "id": "ch35.A.2", "formulas": [], "solution": [{"type": "para", "children": [{"type": "math", "latex": "\\underline{\\hspace{2em}}_{x}"}, {"type": "text", "text": " is within 1 km of "}, {"type": "math", "latex": "\\underline{\\hspace{2em}}_{y}"}]}]}, {"children": [{"type": "para", "children": [{"type": "text", "text": "Transitive, symmetric, but not reflexive"}]}], "id": "ch35.A.3", "formulas": [], "solution": [{"type": "para", "children": [{"type": "math", "latex": "\\underline{\\hspace{2em}}_{x}"}, {"type": "text", "text": " is a full (i.e., not half) sibling of "}, {"type": "math", "latex": "\\underline{\\hspace{2em}}_{y}"}]}]}]}], "items": [{"children": [{"type": "para", "children": [{"type": "text", "text": "Reflexive but not symmetric"}]}], "id": "ch35.A.1", "formulas": [], "solution": [{"type": "para", "children": [{"type": "math", "latex": "\\underline{\\hspace{2em}}_{x}"}, {"type": "text", "text": " is no older than "}, {"type": "math", "latex": "\\underline{\\hspace{2em}}_{y}"}]}]}, {"children": [{"type": "para", "children": [{"type": "text", "text": "Symmetric but not transitive"}]}], "id": "ch35.A.2", "formulas": [], "solution": [{"type": "para", "children": [{"type": "math", "latex": "\\underline{\\hspace{2em}}_{x}"}, {"type": "text", "text": " is within 1 km of "}, {"type": "math", "latex": "\\underline{\\hspace{2em}}_{y}"}]}]}, {"children": [{"type": "para", "children": [{"type": "text", "text": "Transitive, symmetric, but not reflexive"}]}], "id": "ch35.A.3", "formulas": [], "solution": [{"type": "para", "children": [{"type": "math", "latex": "\\underline{\\hspace{2em}}_{x}"}, {"type": "text", "text": " is a full (i.e., not half) sibling of "}, {"type": "math", "latex": "\\underline{\\hspace{2em}}_{y}"}]}]}], "id": "ch35.A", "kind": "free", "sub": null, "logic": "fol", "hasKey": false, "hasSolutions": true}, {"letter": "B", "blocks": [{"type": "para", "children": [{"type": "text", "text": "Show that a relation can be both symmetric and anti-symmetric by giving an interpretation that makes both of the following sentences true:"}]}, {"type": "displaymath", "latex": "& \\forall x\\forall y( R(x,y) \\rightarrow R(y,x))\\\\ & \\forall x\\forall y(( R(x,y) \\land R(y,x)) \\rightarrow x=y)", "env": "align"}], "items": [], "id": "ch35.B", "kind": "free", "sub": null, "logic": "fol", "hasKey": false, "solution": [{"type": "list", "kind": "ekey", "items": [{"label": [{"type": "text", "text": "domain"}], "children": [{"type": "para", "children": [{"type": "math", "latex": "0", "display": false}]}]}, {"label": [{"type": "math", "latex": "R(x,y)"}], "children": [{"type": "para", "children": [{"type": "text", "text": "⟨"}, {"type": "math", "latex": "0", "display": false}, {"type": "text", "text": ", "}, {"type": "math", "latex": "0", "display": false}, {"type": "text", "text": "⟩"}]}]}]}], "hasSolutions": true}], "footnotes": []}